WEBVTT

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.900
A research request?

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:23.500
Yeah.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:28.100
A guy from Hoenn named Hoji
contacted us.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.880
We became friends when we battled
in the Glass Flute Cup!

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.130
What was his request?

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:38.810
Apparently, the water suddenly stopped flowing
at his uncle’s hot spring.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.320
Here’s a photo he sent.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.660
The water?

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.800
And right around that time,
an Absol was seen nearby.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.940
An Absol?

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:53.440
The townspeople suspect the Absol
is why the water stopped.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:57.810
Absol! Disaster Pokémon!
Evil type!

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:01.310
It appears when it senses
an impending natural disaster!

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:04.580
As a result,
it was mistaken as a doom-bringer!

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.040
So, he wants us to
look into the Absol!

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.080
In ancient times, Absol was considered
a doom-bringing Pokémon,

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:16.390
and some people still believe
in that old superstition.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:20.100
So we thought we’d find
the real cause! Right?

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:21.970
Yeah.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:26.570
I see. Well then, you two better go
and help this Hoji!

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:27.850
Right!

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.040
Fuen Town, Hoenn Region

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.580
Satoshi, Go, Pikachu
and Sarunori
Fuen Town, Hoenn Region

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:08.960
have arrived at Fuen Town
in the Hoenn Region.
Fuen Town, Hoenn Region

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.160
have arrived at Fuen Town
in the Hoenn Region.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:14.310
The town’s hot springs are
a famous tourist destination.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.260
Hey!

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.080
There’s Hoji!

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.420
It’s been a while!

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:23.680
You’re here!

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:26.780
That’s a rare one
you’ve got there, Go.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.480
It’s called a Sarunori.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.480
All right, nice to meet you!

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.420
That didn’t hurt! Not one bit!

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:58.340
Good to see you’re both
doing well!

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.560
All the stores are closed...

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.070
Awful, right?

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:12.290
Nobody’s gonna come here
without the hot springs.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:14.770
That sounds rough
for a tourist spot...

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:19.620
Everyone here’s saying
“This is all Absol’s fault!”

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.310
They’re all furious.

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:23.310
Isn’t that just a superstition?

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:26.980
I’ll show ya. C’mon.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.360
What’s this?

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:36.690
Uncle says this tablet’s
been here for generations.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.500
Absol?

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:51.990
Ever since ancient times,
whenever Absol showed up here, disaster followed.

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:57.180
Our ancestors carved this to make sure
the message would be passed down.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.480
See, look at that.

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:04.240
The hot springs must’ve dried up
after Absol appeared in the past, too.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:08.240
So that’s why everyone’s
convinced it’s Absol’s fault...

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:13.090
I don’t really get it,
but everyone’s worried.

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:16.370
So I thought if I asked you,
maybe you could do something.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.500
You’re really kind, Hoji.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.210
S-Save it!

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.720
This is my Uncle’s inn.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.590
Uncle!
What are you doing?!

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:34.850
Oh, Hoji.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:37.600
We’re going Absol hunting.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:38.950
You should join us!

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:40.460
Hunting?!

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.360
We’ve all had enough!

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:46.420
We’re gonna give that Absol a real clobbering,
and bring peace back to our town!

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:47.360
Yeah!

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.520
Hold on a sec!

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:50.830
Who are these kids?

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:55.400
My pals, Satoshi and Go.
And Sarunori and Pikachu.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.710
I had them come here to investigate.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.700
Huh?

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:05.550
I don’t see what
you kids could do to help.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:06.590
What?!

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:11.050
Well, the more hands, the better.
You can come, too.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:15.730
Maybe Absol is just showing itself
to warn you of some danger!

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:17.980
Catching it and getting rid of it
would be wrong!

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.500
What?!

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.020
Why should we listen
to outsiders?!

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:22.980
You got any proof,
any evidence?!

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:27.230
What, you came here to criticize us?

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:28.750
Give us some time!

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:32.100
We’ll investigate,
and uncover the real reason!

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.680
What you’re doing is just cruel to Absol!

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:39.050
Listen to me at least, Uncle.
They know a lot about Pokémon.

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:41.180
They’ll be able to help!

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:47.380
You have two hours. Take any longer,
and we’ll go out hunting!

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.570
It really is empty.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:55.750
Hoji...

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:58.190
When did the water stop?

00:06:58.190 --> 00:07:00.270
About half a month ago, I think?

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:03.350
After Uncle saw
Absol on the mountain,

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:05.450
the water suddenly
cooled down,

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:07.860
then before long,
it was just gone.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:13.950
Fuen Town’s hot springs
come from Mt. Entotsu?

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:18.530
Yeah. The water’s piped from
the source inside the mountain.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:21.600
Everyone here’s afraid of
running into Absol,

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:24.070
so they don’t go near
the source spring.

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:27.590
The water cooling down
is kinda suspicious, too...

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:34.220
Satoshi! Let’s take a look
and see if we can find any clues!

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.270
Okay!

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:39.220
While you’re at it,
I’ll try and convince Uncle.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:42.360
Have him give up that ridiculous idea
of a hunting squad.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:43.870
We’re counting on you, Hoji!

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:45.730
Yeah, leave it to me!

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:49.690
There’s a road winding right to
the spring on Mt. Entotsu.

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:52.490
As long as we follow it,
we can’t get lost.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.820
This is getting kinda fun.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.280
This is pretty rough.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:06.420
Yeah...

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:13.880
All right, we’re nearly there.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:21.230
Absol?!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.070
Look out!

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:29.810
Are you okay?

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:32.610
What are you doing, Absol?!

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.260
Sarunori!

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:55.760
You okay?

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:58.650
Rest up for a bit.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.350
It got away.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.830
Ugh...

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:07.450
What’s wrong with Absol,
attacking us out of nowhere...?

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.400
What now, Go?

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.700
We’ll just have to look for
another path, I guess.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:14.490
Yeah.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:28.090
Pipes!

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:31.550
If we follow these,
they’ll take us to the spring!

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.630
There!

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:37.570
We finally found it.
What a relief!

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:44.950
It’s frozen solid.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:48.270
Then the water stopped
because it was frozen?

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:54.640
But <i>why</i> is it frozen?

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.630
No matter how cold it is,

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:00.030
hot spring water wouldn’t freeze.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:05.790
The water is heated by magma
underground before it surfaces.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:09.160
Does that mean
something’s going on underground?

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:13.610
But how can we
investigate underground...?

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:15.720
I thought this might come up, so...

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:16.760
Go!

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.970
Nuckrar! Dig!

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.330
Looking good!

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:32.270
Nuckrar?

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:35.730
Hey! Did something happen?!

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:40.510
Sorry, Nuckrar...

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:42.450
That must’ve been cold...

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:49.420
It’s frozen...

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:51.490
Something really <i>is</i> wrong!

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.920
Brrr!

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:08.490
What?!

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:09.600
An Onigori?!

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:15.410
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:35.000
Onigori! Face Pokémon!
Ice type!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.470
It has a body of ice that won’t melt,
even with fire!

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:40.800
It can instantly freeze
moisture in the atmosphere!

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:45.640
Pikachu! Electroweb!

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.360
Brrr!

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:58.590
Pikachu, now try―

00:11:58.590 --> 00:11:59.560
Hold on!

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:00.740
Huh? Why?

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:05.050
Don’t you think the Onigori
could be behind the ground freezing?

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:09.160
There could be more of them.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:11.090
Let’s follow it stealthily.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:33.090
A Yukiwarashi!

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:35.230
There really <i>were </i>more of them.

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:40.930
Yukiwarashi! Snow Hat Pokémon!
Ice type!

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:42.990
They can only survive in cold areas!

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.520
They eat snow and ice to survive!

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:49.450
Did that Yukiwarashi
get completely lost and end up here?

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:53.250
This mountain is
too hot for Yukiwarashi.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:57.280
So they froze everything
to make it more comfortable.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.900
That means if we
deal with the Onigori,

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.740
the hot springs should
go back to normal!

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:02.600
All right!

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:04.220
I’ll solve this by catching them!

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:06.800
Absol?!

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:14.950
Wh-Why are you getting
in our way, Absol?!

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:17.560
Just when we got to
the bottom of things...!

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:32.190
Why is Absol attacking us?

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:34.290
Does it have some sorta reason?

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:40.070
I want to trust Absol, too.
I feel the same way you do.

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:41.420
But...

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:43.850
Absol’s eyes earlier...

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:49.840
Maybe Absol appeared
to try and tell us something?!

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:58.070
Hey, Go.
I’m having a hard time here.

00:13:58.070 --> 00:13:59.400
You doing any better?

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:00.580
Yeah.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:05.570
The hot spring stopped because
Onigori arrived and froze the water.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:09.860
Oh, that’s great!
So it really wasn’t Absol.

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:13.200
About that...
I’ve got a favor to ask.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.580
Sure, what is it?

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:20.580
Can you check if that tablet
depicts anything like what’s happening?

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:22.920
Got it, leave it to me!

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:26.900
Sorry, Uncle. We’ll talk more later.
I gotta step out for a bit!

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:33.890
Go...
Why did you ask Hoji to do that?

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:39.960
That tablet depicted all sorts of disasters
that Absol previously warned about.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:43.650
If it shows anything like
what’s currently going on...

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:48.780
Maybe we can figure out
what Absol’s trying to tell us!

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:49.650
Yeah!

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:52.450
Hello?

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:53.780
Go, bingo!

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:57.270
There’s a drawing of
a frozen hot spring on the tablet!

00:14:58.540 --> 00:14:59.190
What is it?

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:04.040
I don’t get why,
but it shows the mountain erupting, too.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:07.140
Does that mean they both
happened at the same time?

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:08.420
Thank you, Hoji!

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:10.140
What is it?

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:12.670
What Absol was trying to tell us...

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:14.430
...was this!

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.680
Huh? An eruption?

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:22.080
300 years ago, Onigori wandered up the mountain
and the hot spring froze.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:26.140
After that, the ice heated up
all at once, made steam...

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:27.740
And the mountain erupted!

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:28.650
Huh?

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:34.700
You know, if steam builds up underground, the pressure rises, right?

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:39.700
Like... If you shake a can of carbonated juice,
it gets full of gas!

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:42.250
What?! That’s awful!

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:46.400
If the ice all melted at once,
the same thing might happen.

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:50.010
That’s why Absol stopped us
from catching the Onigori!

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:52.340
Yeah! We can still make it in time!

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:54.860
What?!

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:58.000
Steam venting!
That could be a sign it’s erupting.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:58.500
Let’s hurry!

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.050
Yeah!

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:11.200
Go... What can we do
to stop the eruption?

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:15.070
We crack the rock open,
and let the steam vent!

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.450
Okay, got it!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.620
Aceburn, go!

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:26.210
Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:38.810
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:45.690
It’s crazy hard!

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:46.650
One more time!

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:47.470
All right!

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:49.320
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!
Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.030
Nothing...

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:02.410
Absol!

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:22.140
We should help!

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:23.180
Yeah!

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.910
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:30.690
Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.320
Okay!

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:46.370
But at this pace...

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:54.240
Absol!

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:54.810
It wouldn’t...

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:03.110
You did it!

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:09.100
Absol!

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:31.130
Absol’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:45.100
Absol, I’m glad you’re okay.

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:51.980
The steam’s stopped venting,
so it looks like everything’s settled down.

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:53.790
So, no eruption?

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:56.250
Nope.
Should be good now, yeah?

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:03.120
Absol. Thank you for
warning us about the disaster.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:05.330
Feel free to go now.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.120
Huh? What is it?

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.550
Wait, is there going to be
another disaster?!

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:26.290
Huh?

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:29.940
Absol’d rather go along with you!

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.700
You... want to come along with me?

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:39.890
Great, huh, Go?

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:46.830
Nice to meet you, Absol!

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:51.980
This feels great.

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:54.400
It’s heavenly, heavenly...

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:56.960
The temperature’s perfect!

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:02.880
It’s good to see
you’re all better, Sarunori.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:05.280
Thanks.

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:08.530
The hot spring’s back,
all because of you.

00:20:08.530 --> 00:20:12.410
And we’ll take the Onigori
somewhere colder.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:14.810
They’d have a hard time
living on Mt. Entotsu, anyway.

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:16.920
Yeah, go ahead.

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:19.260
How’d things go with your uncle?

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.450
He’s given up Absol hunting, right?

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:23.570
Oh, well, about that...

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:26.520
He insisted on doing this.

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:28.450
Please accept my apologies.

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:29.630
Huh?

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:30.560
Water?

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:36.000
Yeah. And the Onigori have been in there,
so it’s freezing cold.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.480
Wh-Why?

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:41.010
I was wrong about Absol,
and about you two.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:46.560
You worked so hard to save our town.
This is the <i>least</i> I can do to apologize!

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.970
I’m sorry!

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:54.770
I was wrong!
Thank you for your help!

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:00.820
Th-That’s enough!
You’ve made your point!

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:02.850
Hurry up and get in the hot spring!

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:06.780
You satisfied now, Uncle?

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:07.820
Yeah.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:12.910
Let’s call it hot water under the bridge,
for the hot spring.

